# Machine-specific paths for this repo. Copy to `.env_vars` and edit.
#
#   cp .env_vars.example .env_vars
#
# `.env_vars` is GITIGNORED, and must stay that way: this repo is PUBLIC, and these are
# absolute paths on your machine. Note it is NOT called `.env` -- `.env` is already the
# general virtualenv DIRECTORY here (see `make env`), so a `.env` file would collide with it.
#
# Format is `VAR=value` (no `export`, no quotes needed), which is both make-includable
# (the Makefile `-include`s this file) and shell-sourceable:
#
#   set -a && . ./.env_vars && set +a

# Where the ORIGINAL track recordings live -- the `NNN-Artist - Title.ext` files that
# `streamalign track-mix` and the origNNN spans in `streamalign hints` correlate against
# the mix. The repo's `sources` symlink points at an external media volume that is often
# not mounted; point this at a copy that is always there.
NETRADIO_SOURCES_DIR=/Users/timh/Downloads/Netradio/sources
